{"pc": "0x80156352", "binary": "WORLD.BIN", "kind": "PLATE", "text": "Glove-cursor bob IDLE table  (glove_cursor_bob_idle_table)  [ADR-0046]\n------------------------------------------------------------\nWorld-map / menu hand-cursor at-rest bob. Encoding differs from the tile\ncursor: [threshold, signed offset] byte-pairs, 0-terminated (a threshold\nof 0 ends the table), indexed by a modulo timer.\nidle = (16,0)(18,1)(22,2)(28,3)(36,2)(46,1)  ; cumulative-threshold ramp\nOffset is a SIGNED byte (can go negative -- see the select table). Same\nbob CONCEPT as the tile cursor, different timing model. Parsed into\ncursor_bob.json as glove_idle; no Godot consumer yet (gh #73)."}
{"pc": "0x80156362", "binary": "WORLD.BIN", "kind": "PLATE", "text": "Glove-cursor bob SELECT table  (glove_cursor_bob_select_table)  [ADR-0046]\n------------------------------------------------------------\nThe select-state variant of the glove-cursor bob. Same [threshold, signed\noffset] byte-pair, 0-terminated encoding as the idle table.\nselect = (2,0)(8,-2)(10,1)(12,3)(14,5)(16,4)(18,3)(24,2)(34,1)(36,0)(38,0)\nNote the SIGNED offset (8,-2): the select bob dips negative, proving the\noffset byte is int8, not unsigned. Parsed into cursor_bob.json as\nglove_select; deferred consumer (gh #73)."}
